  "checked": null,
  "source": "\"Daily Express\" Community Song Book, collected and edited by John Goss (The London Express Newspaper, London, 1927), p. 195, \"London's Burning\", a round for four voices, its lines numbered 1 to 4 for the entries and 4, 3, 2, 1 at their ends, read here as where each voice stops so all finish together, in G, written here a whole tone lower in F; read from the scan at archive.org/details/bwb_KU-674-294 (leaf n198). John Goss died in 1953."
